# Paths the OpenWiki doc agent must not read, document, or cite.
#
# This file is load-bearing for run time, not just tidiness: OpenWiki has no
# .gitignore support of any kind, so without these rules the agent can reach
# ~192k files under node_modules/ alone (against 489 tracked files). Activating
# any rule here also enables OpenWiki's guard against unbounded root globs.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-style and last-match-wins.

# Dependencies and build output.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Secrets. Gitignored, so absent from CI checkouts, but present on disk for
# local `openwiki` runs — these must never be quoted into a generated page.
.env.local
.env*.local
requests/http-client.private.env.json

# Design bundle and handoff artifacts, ported verbatim from the design bundle.
# Excluded from lint/build and protected by .claude/hooks/protect-static-dirs.sh.
assets/
preview/
screenshots/
ui_kits/
uploads/
FIGMA FILES/
diagrams/
.design-sync/

# ...except the design-system spec itself, which lives under uploads/ and is
# real evidence, not a ported artifact: design-system.md cites it as the
# upstream source that says WCAG 2.1 AA where RULES.md demands 2.2 AA.
# Excluding it made the evidence resolver hard-fail on an existing Claim and
# killed the whole run. The 2.6 MB PDF beside it stays out.
!uploads/training-compliance-design-system.md

# Hand-maintained Obsidian vault notes whose titles mirror the OpenWiki
# taxonomy. Claims belong grounded in code, not in parallel prose that drifts.
wiki/

# Vendored third-party skill reference docs, not app code.
.claude/skills/

# Editor and tooling local state.
.idea/
.vscode/
